        'readiness_slug' => 'trl-8-9',
        'readiness_label' => 'TRL 8',
        'short_description' => 'ADBASTER is a next-generation outdoor advertising technology that redefines the very concept of an advertising surface.',
        'seo_title' => 'ADBASTER | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ADBASTER is a next-generation outdoor advertising technology that redefines the very concept of an advertising surface.',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ADBASTER is a next-generation outdoor advertising technology that redefines the very concept of an advertising surface. Instead of constructing new media structures or deploying capital-intensive LED screens, ADBASTER converts existing physical surfaces into multi-channel digital advertising platforms using compact laser projection. The system replaces conventional billboard floodlights with a weather-resistant digital laser projector capable of rendering full-color, high-contrast imagery directly onto walls, billboards, façades, and other large surfaces. Content is delivered via the internet and can be updated dynamically — by the minute if required. ADBASTER addresses the core structural limitation of traditional outdoor advertising: one surface = one advertiser. By enabling time-based multiplexing, it allows a single physical surface to host multiple advertisers simultaneously, increasing revenue density while reducing costs for advertisers. It introduces a new class of advertising surface — virtually multiplexed, digitally controlled, and economically scalable.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Existing billboard networks (direct retrofit, no downtime, immediate revenue uplift); urban façades and walls (monetization of previously unused city surfaces); temporary events and campaigns (rapid deployment without construction or permits); SME advertising access (enables small and medium businesses to use large formats); smart city deployments (dynamic public messaging plus commercial content).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>A compact digital laser projector is installed at the existing floodlight mount and projects full-color, high-contrast imagery directly onto any flat or semi-flat surface. Content is delivered over the internet in real time and can be changed within seconds to minutes. Time-based multiplexing splits the projection schedule between many advertisers, so a single surface serves 10–100+ advertisers instead of one. Monetization logic shifts from static area-based rent to dynamic time-and-attention-based revenue.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>| Parameter | ADBASTER value | Traditional billboard / LED |</p>
<p>|---|---|---|</p>
<p>| Projection technology | Digital laser projection | Printed posters / LED matrix |</p>
<p>| Installation point | Existing floodlight mount | New structure / reinforced frame |</p>
<p>| Surface requirements | Any flat or semi-flat surface | Special screen or construction |</p>
<p>| Content delivery | Internet (real-time) | Manual replacement / media server |</p>
<p>| Content update rate | Seconds to minutes | Weeks (posters) / fixed loops (LED) |</p>
<p>| Simultaneous advertisers | 10–100+ (time-sliced) | 1 (billboard) / limited (LED) |</p>
<p>| Energy consumption | ~80 W | Billboard lighting 400–1,000 W / LED 10–15 kW |</p>
<p>| Weather resistance | All-weather, vandal-safe | Medium (posters) / high-maintenance (LED) |</p>
<p>| Maintenance | Very low | Medium to very high |</p>
<p>| Urban footprint | None (no new structures) | High (visual and physical) |</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Weather-resistant, vandal-safe digital laser projector mounted at the existing billboard floodlight position; internet-based content delivery and scheduling; time-multiplexing content management. No new structures, foundations, or LED panels required.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Environmental and urban: zero printed media (eliminates paper, plastics, inks, transport, and poster waste); no new structures, preserving city architecture and skyline; ultra-low energy use, orders of magnitude below LED screens; reduced visual pollution — content exists only when projected; lower regulatory friction, minimal permitting. Economic: revenue multiplication — a single surface can generate 5–10× higher annual revenue through advertiser multiplexing; CapEx efficiency (no new billboard construction, no LED panels, no foundations); OpEx reduction; advertiser cost reduction of up to 60% versus classic billboard placement. Strategic: transforms outdoor advertising from a capital-heavy static asset business into a dynamic digital media platform, lowering entry barriers and expanding the advertiser base. For surface owners it replaces fixed monthly rent with scalable revenue; for advertisers it replaces static posters with adaptive messaging; for cities it replaces visual clutter with controlled, reversible media.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Arbok-SmartCity-Core — adaptive urban infrastructure · Arbok-Energy-Light — ultra-low-power lighting systems · Arbok-EdgeControl — remote content and asset management · Arbok-UrbanShield — vandal-resistant city hardware</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Retrofit onto existing billboard floodlight mounts with no downtime; no structural changes and minimal permitting. Content is managed and updated remotely over the internet. Maintenance is very low.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 8–9</strong> — System fully engineered, field-tested, and validated in urban environments. Commercial rollout-ready with proven economic performance.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>Existing billboard networks, urban façades and walls, event and campaign advertising, SME advertisers previously priced out of large formats, and smart city deployments. [требует уточнения из базы — количественный объём рынка]</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>Revenue multiplication of 5–10× per surface through advertiser multiplexing; typical ROI of 4–8 months per surface in conservative scenarios; advertiser monthly spend up to 60% lower than classic billboard placement; energy consumption ~80 W versus 400–1,000 W for billboard lighting and 10–15 kW for LED.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Risk Factors</h2><p>[требует уточнения из базы]</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Related Technologies</h2><p>Arbok-SmartCity-Core · Arbok-Energy-Light · Arbok-EdgeControl · Arbok-UrbanShield</p></section>',
