        'short_description' => 'ARBOK-3X is a pulsed UVC sanitization system that extends the shelf life of packaged perishables by 20–50 % using high-intensity pulsed UVC irradiation from a xenon flash lamp source.',
        'seo_title' => 'ARBOK FOOD PRESERVATION (ARBOK-3X) | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-3X is a pulsed UVC sanitization system that extends the shelf life of packaged perishables by 20–50 % using high-intensity pulsed UVC irradiation from…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-3X is a pulsed UVC sanitization system that extends the shelf life of packaged perishables by 20–50 % using high-intensity pulsed UVC irradiation from a xenon flash lamp source. Non-contact and ambient-temperature, it lets supermarkets, distribution centers, and warehouses cut food waste, improve profitability, and enhance food safety — with no chemicals, consumables, or residue. Core idea: &quot;Save to Earn&quot; — every 1 % reduction in food loss is direct economic gain.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Pre-packaging and post-harvest sanitization on production lines; bulk treatment of high-volume SKUs at distribution centers; on-site freshness extension before retail display; complement to cold storage/logistics. Mountable as conveyor integration, UV tunnel, or static chamber.</p>
<p>Users: retailers, distribution/logistics operators, food processors.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Pulsed UVC light damages microbial DNA/RNA, inactivating spoilage organisms (Erwinia, Pseudomonas, Botrytis cinerea, molds, yeasts, fungal spores). Pulsed delivery gives high-intensity treatment without overheating, with exposure time per item tuned short enough to keep line throughput fast. Treated products retain color, texture, and nutrition. Non-contact, ambient temperature.</p>
<p>Limitations: surface treatment only (line-of-sight UVC; shadowed areas untreated); does not penetrate opaque packaging; complements but does not replace refrigeration.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Xenon pulsed-UVC flash lamp source, sized to the application; conveyor / UV-tunnel / static-chamber housing; control and exposure timing; non-contact treatment zone. Plug-and-play, modular integration into existing lines/stores.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Technical: broad-spectrum pathogen coverage; non-contact; no overheating; retains product quality. Economic: ultra-low OPEX (&lt;$0.001/kg), no consumables, ROI &lt;12 months. Environmental: no chemicals/water/packaging waste, no residue, prevents landfill methane. Competitive: vs traditional sanitizers — no consumables/residue, broad spectrum, non-contact.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Drop-in for production lines, DCs, retail, and cold-storage hubs; conveyor/tunnel/chamber form factors; complements refrigeration and ARBOK FoodTech retail platforms.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Rapid plug-and-play deployment; site evaluation → installation → staff training → ROI modeling/monitoring. Customizable integration into existing lines or stores.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 7 (confirmed by Michael).</strong> Prototype/system in operational environment: validated by retailers and logistics partners and positioned commercial-ready, with broader multi-site deployment/qualification remaining. (Legacy &quot;TRL 9&quot; set to 7 per Michael.)</p>
<p>TRL scale:</p>
