</ul></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>Retail food waste is enormous (often ~30 % spoilage on fresh produce). A non-contact, consumable-free shelf-life extender with sub-12-month ROI addresses supermarkets, distribution, and post-harvest globally. Example: a retailer with $10M/year fruit sales and 30 % spoilage ($3M) saving 50 % = $1.5M/year.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>OPEX &lt;$0.001/kg (no consumables); ROI &lt;12 months for an average distribution center; retail savings ~15 % of revenue via up-to-50 % waste reduction. Payback example: $1.5M/year savings on $10M fruit sales.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Risk Factors</h2><p>Per-product shelf-life and savings claims need independent validation. Surface/line-of-sight limitation (shadowed produce untreated); no penetration of opaque packaging. UVC operational safety (shielding). Adoption depends on retailer integration and validation. Legacy TRL adjusted down pending multi-site qualification.</p></section>
