<p>Leachate enters a deep-vacuum chamber where water evaporates at ambient temperature; no contaminants enter the vapor phase. Vapor condenses to clean water; salts, organics, ammonium, metals, and microplastics remain as dry residue. Pathogens rupture under vacuum collapse — no UV, chlorine, or ozone. No membranes, filters, or reagents at any stage.</p>
