<p>• Standard industrial electrical supply</p>
<p>• 24/7 continuous operation; minimal operator presence</p>
<p>Installation timeline:</p>
<p>• 4–8 weeks per module to operational state</p>
<p>• Pilot phase: 6–9 months including peat-type matrix testing</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p>TRL 5–6 (peat-specific) — to be reviewed and confirmed by ARBOK</p>
<p>Evidence basis:</p>
<p>• Arbok-VC and AZOW platforms (TRL 8–9) operate on the same physical principles — deep vacuum, ambient temperature, water-from-organic-matrix separation — and are commercially deployed for produced water, sewage, biogas digestate, and pyrolysis liquid</p>
<p>• AZOW briquettes from organic concentrate already certified at 14–20 MJ/kg, comparable to lignite</p>
<p>• Peat-specific extension is a feedstock adaptation, not a new physical principle</p>
<p>Remaining steps:</p>
