        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-BLACKSAND uses thermodynamic phase-change separation to remediate oil and petroleum-product spills from water, sand, and soil — including contaminated surface and subsurface waters (lakes, rivers, seas) and their sediments. It splits the mixture into clean reusable water, dry solids (sand, soil), and recovered oil/petroleum (returned to storage or pipelines), with no chemicals, filters, membranes, or reagents.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Primary use cases: cleanup of oil-water-sand/soil mixtures; contaminated sediment treatment; spill emergencies at ports, pipelines, wells, and refineries; industrial wastewater.</p>
