<p>Acidic mine water (pH &lt; 2.5) is fed to a vacuum chamber; only water evaporates at ambient temperature and condenses to clean water, while metals (Fe, Al, Zn, Cu), sulfates, and acidity concentrate in the residue. The residue is immobilized into concrete-like mineral matrices for dry, isolated deposition. An optional alkali conditioning step, using standard neutralizing agents, sets discharge pH when required. No membranes.</p>
