        'short_description' => 'ARBOK-COIN (AC) is an advanced computational optimization system designed to radically reduce the computational and energy cost of cryptocurrency mining by narrowing the effective search space required for hash generation.',
        'seo_title' => 'ARBOK-COIN (AC) | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-COIN (AC) is an advanced computational optimization system designed to radically reduce the computational and energy cost of cryptocurrency mining by…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-COIN (AC) is an advanced computational optimization system designed to radically reduce the computational and energy cost of cryptocurrency mining by narrowing the effective search space required for hash generation. The core objective is to eliminate redundant brute-force computation inherent in classical mining architectures. By constraining the solution space at a fundamental algorithmic level, the system reduces the required number of hash attempts by more than one million times, resulting in a proportional reduction in time, energy consumption, and hardware load. Unlike traditional mining solutions that rely on increasing raw computational power, ARBOK-COIN focuses on computational selectivity — reducing what must be calculated rather than accelerating everything indiscriminately. It is designed as a core technology, intended for exclusive use or controlled licensing rather than mass-market hardware deployment.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Optimized cryptocurrency mining operations; mining in regions with high electricity costs; private or sovereign mining infrastructure; licensing-based market control strategies.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Reduction of the effective computation range: the hash search space is constrained at a fundamental algorithmic level, narrowing it by more than 1,000,000×. This proportionally reduces time, energy consumption, and hardware load, and enables economically viable mining even in regions with high electricity costs and limited infrastructure.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>| Parameter | Value (conceptual) |</p>
<p>|---|---|</p>
<p>| System type | Computational optimization / mining acceleration |</p>
<p>| Core principle | Reduction of effective computation range |</p>
<p>| Computation reduction | &gt; 1,000,000× narrowing of hash search space |</p>
<p>| Energy efficiency | Up to 100× lower energy consumption per hash vs conventional mining |</p>
<p>| Supported assets | Adaptable to multiple cryptocurrency protocols; specific compatibility defined during implementation |</p>
<p>| Footprint | Compact architecture; final form factor defined during industrial design |</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Compact architecture; final form factor to be defined during industrial design. Delivered as a core technology for exclusive use or controlled licensing rather than mass-market hardware.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Mining speed significantly increased due to reduced computation domain. Lower thermal load and reduced cooling requirements. Enables stable operation in high electricity cost regions. Reduces dependency on large-scale mining farms. Environmental: drastically reduced power consumption; lower carbon footprint per mined unit; no requirement for large energy infrastructure; supports sustainable digital asset production.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>ARBOK-COMPUTE · ARBOK-ENERGY-OPTIMIZATION · ARBOK-DIGITAL-INFRA</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Implementation framework: partner acquires exclusive core technology rights for €1,000,000; ARBOK engineering team performs industrial design and system realization; development timeline ~16 weeks; production location Israel; post-deployment revenue sharing from mining and licensing activities. No mandatory infrastructure overhaul required. Offer validity: 6 months.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 3–4</strong> — Concept validated through preliminary testing. Initial results confirm &gt;1,000,000× computation reduction and ~100× energy efficiency gains. Industrial design and full system validation pending.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>Mining operations in electricity-expensive jurisdictions; private or sovereign mining infrastructure; licensing-based market control. Revenue streams: direct cryptocurrency mining, licensing of technology to third parties, controlled market participation via exclusivity.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>Core technology rights: €1,000,000 (one-time). No mandatory infrastructure overhaul required. OPEX impact: energy consumption reduced by ~100×; mining remains profitable where traditional systems are not. Profit model: mining profits and licensing revenues distributed according to agreed shares; high ROI potential in electricity-expensive jurisdictions.</p></section>
