<p><strong>ARBOK OPEX breakdown:</strong> electricity $230,000–$384,000 per year (including the up-to-20% grid reduction from TERU) plus service $200,000–$300,000 per year; continuous water cost $0 per year.</p>
<p>Additional cost items not quantified in the source (dry residue disposal, module replacement, insurance):</p>',
            'use_cases' => '<p>Cooling towers and cooling fields exist at thermal power plants, refineries, metallurgy, chemicals, pulp and paper, large compressor stations, data centers, and cold-storage terminals — different shapes, same mission: dump low-grade heat produced as a byproduct of the main process while keeping circulating water temperature inside a strict corridor.</p>
<ul>
<li>Replacement of classic wet cooling towers, fan-section fields, channels and ponds.</li>
<li>Nuclear and thermal power plants facing summer curtailment: rivers become shallow and warm, cooling water is insufficient, and heated water cannot legally be returned above temperature limits.</li>
<li>Sites with aerosol, sanitary, or Legionella regulatory exposure (nuclear plants, refineries, data centers, hospitals, hotels).</li>
<li>Sites where water is scarce, expensive, or subject to abstraction restrictions.</li>
</ul>
<p>The unit runs 24/7. If cooling fails, performance drops fast, restrictions kick in, and in the worst case the facility stops.</p>
<ul>
<li>Delivered as modular container-type equipment; capacity is scaled by the number of identical modules.</li>
<li>Water is filled once; there is no continuous makeup and no discharge.</li>
<li>Operates 24/7, with the reference economics based on 8,000 hours per year.</li>
<li>ARBOK-Sonar runs continuous monitoring; on deviation the unit alerts operators or moves to protective mode up to shutdown.</li>
<li>Ongoing operational tasks: scheduled service (budgeted at $200,000–$300,000 per year at the reference scale) and handling of the dry solid residue produced by water cleaning.</li>
<li>The source notes that at high delta the timeline is set by how quickly the site can accept the new equipment.</li>
</ul>
<p>Installation duration, commissioning procedure, staffing: [требует уточнения из базы]</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>ARBOK-Sonar</strong> — mandatory 24/7 water quality and recirculation control, with data transmission to the control center and automatic protective shutdown on deviation.</li>
<li><strong>ARBOK-TERU</strong> — parasitic heat recovery component of the unit, reducing grid electricity draw by up to 20%.</li>
<li><strong>Plant side:</strong> connects to condensers and heat exchangers in place of the classic wet tower circuit.</li>
</ul>
<p>Interfaces to plant SCADA/DCS, retrofit sequencing on existing sites: [требует уточнения из базы]</p>',
