<p>Outputs/uses: stable synthetic fuel (storable, transportable, refinable); methane and hydrogen (on-site use or sale); separable product fractions.</p>
<p>Industries and users: refiners, pyrolysis-plant operators, waste-to-fuel hubs.</p>
<p>Scale: 100–150 tons/day per vertical 20-ft container; mobile.</p>
<p>Steps: feed assay → unit sizing → containerized install → commissioning. Continuous, autonomous, minimal maintenance; mobile redeployment.</p>
<p>Pairs with Arbok-Pyrolysis (upstream oil) and ARBOK-VC (upgrading); methane/hydrogen to on-site energy; product fractions to fuel/chemical buyers.</p>',
