<p>Industries and users: off-grid/niche power, research, resilient installations.</p>
<p>Scale: ~1 kW prototype; linearly scalable by tube count, field, flow, or module stacking.</p>',
            'solution' => '<p>ARBOK-LIQUID GEN is a compact electrical generator using liquid-metal electromagnetic induction — no copper windings, no mechanical rotation. A conductive liquid (Galinstan) is pumped through a static, non-uniform magnetic field, inducing an EMF along the flow (Faraday&#x27;s law), with no moving solid parts. Deliberately non-hyped: classical electrodynamics, no exotic materials or high-speed rotors — prioritizing reliability, silence, low maintenance, and workshop-level manufacturability.</p>
