<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>Palm-oil producing regions (e.g. Indonesia, claimed ~10 million t/year demand) face diesel cost and logistics burdens; a low-cost solid fuel from local oil — if validated — addresses military, off-grid, and export-fuel segments while monetizing oleochemical by-products.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>Claimed total cost ~$25/t, combining operating cost, capital amortization and logistics, vs diesel ~$920/t total; gross savings ~$895/t. Macro example: Indonesia ~$8.9 billion/year. Figures indicative; contingent on validated palm-fuel performance.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Risk Factors</h2><p>Application unproven for palm-oil solid fuel despite mature CC platform. Solid fuel handling/combustion certification needed. Lower energy density than diesel (40 vs 45 MJ/kg). Cost and macro-savings claims aggressive and unvalidated. Feedstock (palm oil) sustainability/regulatory scrutiny. Legacy TRL overstated.</p></section>
