<p>The program runs the sargassum cycle: (1) remove phosphate runoff entering the ocean (eliminate root cause); (2) remediate phosphogypsum stockpiles (1 billion+ tons in Florida); (3) deploy ARBOK purification at river mouths and coastlines; (4) collect and convert seaweed + sludge into fertilizers/biofuel; (5) remove heavy metals and arsenic via TAS-based acid conversion. Each step uses an existing ARBOK component technology.</p>
