        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>For the whole history of the internal combustion engine the spark plug has been the component that ignites the air-fuel mixture, and its presence dictates cylinder-head geometry, service intervals and a class of failure modes. SparkFire removes it.</p>
<p>Ignition is produced by non-contact action on the fuel, generating the spark by alternative means rather than across an electrode gap. The consequence is not only a simpler engine: the source states that combustion efficiency improves, fuel economy improves and emissions fall, and that the change reaches the operating principles and operating modes of the equipment rather than being a component substitution.</p>
<p>The status recorded in the source is Concept.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Internal combustion engines across their range of uses — the source describes the advance as applicable to engine efficiency and performance &quot;in a variety of applications&quot; without naming a lead sector.</p>
<p>Specific target segments, engine classes and first application: [требует уточнения из базы].</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>The air-fuel mixture is ignited without spark plugs. Sparks are generated by alternative means of non-contact action on the fuel, which removes the electrode gap and with it the requirement to route high voltage to a wear part inside the combustion chamber.</p>
<p>Eliminating the plug simplifies engine design and changes its functionality — the source frames this as a change of principle rather than of part.</p>
<p>Physical mechanism of the non-contact spark generation, energy source, timing control and how the effect is localized in the chamber: [требует уточнения из базы].</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>| Parameter | Value |</p>
<p>|---|---|</p>
<p>| Ignition method | non-contact action on fuel; no spark plugs |</p>
<p>| Effect on combustion efficiency | improved — quantification [требует уточнения из базы] |</p>
<p>| Effect on fuel economy | improved — quantification [требует уточнения из базы] |</p>
<p>| Effect on emissions | reduced — quantification [требует уточнения из базы] |</p>
<p>| Status | Concept |</p>
<p>| Energy demand, timing range, ignition energy, engine speed limits | [требует уточнения из базы] |</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>The spark plug and its high-voltage circuit are removed and replaced by the non-contact ignition means. Cylinder-head design is simplified accordingly.</p>
<p>Equipment composition, control electronics and integration with existing engine management: [требует уточнения из базы].</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p><strong>Design.</strong> No spark plugs, therefore no electrode wear, no plug replacement interval and no high-voltage lead into the chamber. Engine design is simplified.</p>
<p><strong>Performance.</strong> Combustion efficiency and fuel economy improve, and emissions fall, per the source.</p>
<p><strong>Scope of change.</strong> The source presents the technology as altering the principles and modes of engine operation, not as a drop-in part.</p>
