        'seo_title' => 'ARBOK-SUGAR | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-SUGAR applies ARBOK-VC (vacuum evaporation at ambient temperature) to sugar juice concentration, replacing traditional multi-effect evaporators that…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-SUGAR applies ARBOK-VC (vacuum evaporation at ambient temperature) to sugar juice concentration, replacing traditional multi-effect evaporators that require 200 years of fossil-fuel-intensive heating. Operating at deep vacuum and ambient temperature, ARBOK evaporates water from raw sugar juice without thermal damage, eliminates bacterial/pathogenic contamination in a single pass, and delivers pre-crystallized syrup at 60–65 % dry solids. Energy consumption drops 15–40× (from 20–80 kWh/t to 2–5 kWh/t); capital and operating costs collapse; water recovered and recycled in-process.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Primary use cases: sugar juice concentration (replacing multi-effect evaporators); water recovery and reuse in sugar mills; pathogen elimination without heat damage.</p>
<p>Industries and users: cane sugar mills, beet sugar factories, small to large-scale producers.</p>
<p>Scale: modular units 50–500 t/day feedstock per unit; stackable for facility capacity.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Raw sugar juice (cane or beet) enters a vacuum chamber where water evaporates at ambient temperature under deep vacuum, dropping the boiling point from 100 °C to ambient temperature. Water vapor is condensed separately and recovered for reuse; the concentrated syrup (60–65 % dry solids) is extracted nearly crystallized. Simultaneously, the vacuum environment kills bacteria and pathogens instantly (no viable organisms survive vacuum). Unlike traditional multi-effect evaporators (heating at 40–80 °C across multiple stages, causing caramelization and nutrient loss), ARBOK preserves sugar quality, eliminates thermal stress, and completes concentration in a single pass.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>Feedstock: raw sugar juice (cane or beet), 10–15 % dry solids input.</p>
<p>Output: concentrated syrup 60–65 % dry solids, near-crystallized, ready for final crystallization.</p>
<p>Energy: 2–5 kWh/t feedstock (vs. 20–80 kWh/t traditional multi-effect evaporators).</p>
<p>Processing time: continuous, 24/7 automated operation.</p>
<p>Water recovery: 100 % clean, potable-grade, recycled in-mill.</p>
<p>Microbial elimination: 100 % (vacuum-instant kill).</p>
<p>Throughput: 50–500 t/day per unit, modular.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Vacuum evaporation chamber; condensation/water recovery system; syrup extraction module; PLC/automation. Modular, standard containerized design; operates on standard power supply; integrates into existing mill infrastructure.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Technical: single-pass concentration; no heat damage; pathogen elimination without chemicals; water recovery; composition-independent (works with all sugar sources).</p>
<p>Economic: energy savings €10–40 per ton of feedstock; simplified mill workflow (eliminates 3–5 multi-effect stages); reduced capital (smaller footprint, no complex heating systems); payback 3–5 years.</p>
<p>Environmental: 15–40× lower energy → 15–40× lower CO₂; zero chemical additives; closed-loop water; zero discharge.</p>
<p>Quality: sugar color/purity improved (no caramelization); taste/aroma preservation; meets premium standards.</p>
<p>Strategic: enables energy-independent sugar production in regions with expensive or unstable power; eligible for ESG/carbon credits.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Retrofits to existing sugar mills (replaces multi-effect evaporator array); water recovery fed to process/cooling loops; condensate recycled back to feedstock preparation.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Deployment begins with juice characterization (feed source and impurity profile), followed by unit sizing, installation (typically 4–8 weeks), and commissioning with integration into existing crystallization/centrifugation equipment. Continuous operation, automated, minimal labor (1 technician per shift).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p>TRL 7 — pilot/demonstration scale validated in sugar mill trials. Multi-ton batches of raw juice processed; final syrup quality confirmed equivalent or superior to traditional multi-effect output; energy savings and water recovery measured and validated. Ready for commercial deployment at mid-scale (100–300 t/day feedstock) with established sugar mills.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>Global sugar production ~180 million tons/year; energy costs account for 20–30 % of manufacturing cost. Traditional multi-effect evaporators dominate but are energy-intensive relics. ARBOK-SUGAR addresses ≥50 % of capacity globally over 10 years = ~90 M tons/year processing; energy savings alone = $900 M–$3.6 B/year industry-wide. Early adoption in cane-heavy regions (Brazil, India, Indonesia); cost-sensitive beet producers (EU, USA).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>Per 200 t/day feedstock unit: energy savings €40 000–160 000/yr; simplified operations (fewer staff, less maintenance) €20 000–40 000/yr; water reuse value €10 000–20 000/yr. Total annual benefit €70 000–220 000; CAPEX payback 3–5 years. Modular scaling: 50 t/day units for smaller mills (~€15 000–50 000/yr benefit).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Risk Factors</h2><p>Sugar mill operators&#x27; conservatism (multi-effect evaporators are established); integration complexity with existing crystallization workflows; feedstock variability (pH, impurity load) requiring process tuning. Requires documentary proof-of-concept in sugar-mill environment with established producers.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Related Technologies</h2><p>ARBOK-VC (Vacuum Cracking) · ARBOK-COFFEE · ARBOK-DEALCO · ARBOK TEXTILE-WASTE</p></section>',
