        'sector_name' => 'Organic Fertilizers',
        'readiness_slug' => 'trl-8-9',
        'readiness_label' => 'TRL 9',
        'short_description' => 'ARBOK-Stone-Fruit-Sharka applies the Arbok-Repeel acid agent to protect Prunus stone fruit from Plum Pox Virus (Sharka, PPV) — the most dangerous stone-fruit virus and quarantine object #1, with no cure (infected trees are uprooted).',
        'seo_title' => 'ARBOK-Stone-Fruit-Sharka | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-Stone-Fruit-Sharka applies the Arbok-Repeel acid agent to protect Prunus stone fruit from Plum Pox Virus (Sharka, PPV) — the most dangerous stone-fruit…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-Stone-Fruit-Sharka applies the Arbok-Repeel acid agent to protect Prunus stone fruit from Plum Pox Virus (Sharka, PPV) — the most dangerous stone-fruit virus and quarantine object #1, with no cure (infected trees are uprooted). PPV is spread by 20+ aphid species via near-instant non-persistent transmission plus infected planting material. Repeel&#x27;s strength is repellence, not killing: the aphid does not land or probe the leaf, so it cannot transmit the virus — exactly what&#x27;s needed against instant transmission — while remaining safe for the pollinators stone fruit needs to set.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Repellent spraying of orchards and nurseries during aphid flight season; priority on nurseries and certified planting-material plots to stop the virus leaving with saplings/grafts; complements (not replaces) clean planting material and removal of diseased trees.</p>
<p>Users: stone-fruit growers, nurseries, certification programs (peach/plum/apricot belts: Mediterranean, China, etc.).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>The Repeel acid mist makes aphids avoid landing/probing treated leaves, narrowing the PPV infection channel against its near-instant non-persistent transmission. Pollinator-safe (essential for fruit set); residual acid neutralizes to water and safe salts.</p>
<p>Limitations: virus not cured — value via vector pressure reduction + clean material + rogueing; aphid transmission is instant, so timely area-wide application matters; stone-fruit-specific field validation pending.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>Agent: Arbok-Repeel acid solution from phosphate waste (&gt;6 billion t globally). Action: aphids avoid landing; pollinator-safe; soil-neutralizing. Application: area-wide repellent spray in aphid-flight season; priority nurseries/mother stock. Cost: ~€40–90/ha per pass. Platform production (Arbok-VC): deep vacuum, ambient temperature, 2–4 kWh/t feed, zero effluent.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Repeel concentrate (Arbok-VC) undergoes dilution and dosing before application via orchard/nursery sprayer or drone; supported by aphid-flight monitoring, clean planting-material certification and diseased-tree rogueing protocol, and PPE/acid handling.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Technical: repellence prevents landing/probing — the only effective lever against instant non-persistent transmission; pollinator-safe. Economic: ~€40–90/ha per pass vs orchard loss of €40,000–80,000/ha (including lost revenue). Environmental: pollinator-safe, soil-buffered, phosphate-waste origin.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Application of Arbok-Repeel; fits orchard IPM, nursery certification, and quarantine programs; sibling to other Repeel/TRINITY crop cards.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Area-wide repellent spraying in aphid-flight season, prioritizing nurseries/mother stock; paired with clean planting material and removal of diseased trees. Remaining: stone-fruit-specific field validation and protocol standardization.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 5 (confirmed by Michael).</strong> Validated in relevant environment at the agent level (Repeel proven on related chitin pests), with stone-fruit/aphid-specific field validation pending.</p>
<p>TRL scale:</p>
<ul>
<li>TRL 1 — basic principles observed</li>
<li>TRL 2 — technology concept formulated</li>
<li>TRL 3 — experimental proof-of-concept</li>
<li>TRL 4 — validated in lab</li>
<li><strong>TRL 5 — validated in relevant environment ← ARBOK-Stone-Fruit-Sharka</strong></li>
<li>TRL 6 — demonstrated in relevant environment</li>
<li>TRL 7 — prototype in operational environment</li>
<li>TRL 8 — system complete and qualified</li>
<li>TRL 9 — proven in operational environment</li>
</ul></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p>PPV hits Prunus at scale: peaches/nectarines ~25–26 Mt/year, plums ~12 Mt/year, apricots ~4 Mt/year; marketable-fruit loss up to 80–100 % and cumulative damage &gt;€10 billion over 30 years. Europe/Mediterranean is the epicenter; China is the largest producer; North America shows eradication is possible via strict quarantine. A pollinator-safe vector repellent — if validated — supports orchard and nursery protection where no cure exists.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Typical Project Economics</h2><p>Establishing a new stone-fruit orchard costs €15,000–30,000/ha plus 3–4 years to first marketable yield; with lost revenue a lost orchard is €40,000–80,000/ha. Area-wide repellent ~€40–90/ha per pass, several passes/season — orders of magnitude cheaper than orchard loss. Agent feedstock negative-cost phosphate waste.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Risk Factors</h2><p>Virus not cured — depends on vector reduction + clean material + rogueing. Instant non-persistent transmission demands timely, area-wide coverage. Stone-fruit field efficacy needs validation. Quarantine/regulatory frameworks per region. Acid handling/PPE.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Related Technologies</h2><p>Arbok-Repeel · ARBOK-Cucurbits-Triple-Strike · ARBOK-Potato · ARBOK-Tomato-Pepper</p></section>',
