        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-TURBIO is a compact, closed-cycle mini-hydropower plant designed to generate up to 50 kWh of electricity autonomously.',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-TURBIO is a compact, closed-cycle mini-hydropower plant designed to generate up to 50 kWh of electricity autonomously. The system operates using water as the working fluid in a fully closed loop, without the need for a natural water source or external water flow. The main innovation lies in its self-sustaining hydroelectric loop: once activated using any available external power (grid, diesel generator, solar panels, or wind turbines), the system maintains energy production without additional input or fuel. It requires no combustion, no emissions, and no external water replenishment. The installation is approximately the size of a 40-foot container and houses the entire generator system. The technology aims to provide a green, autonomous, and stable power supply where conventional grids are unavailable, unreliable, or environmentally unsuitable.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Residential homes or apartment blocks; off-grid locations or remote facilities; industrial operations needing backup or supplementary power.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Water circulates as the working fluid in a fully closed hydroelectric loop. Startup uses any available external power source — grid, diesel generator, solar panels, or wind turbines — after which the loop is self-sustaining and maintains energy production without further input or fuel. No combustion, no emissions, and no external water replenishment.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>| Parameter | Value |</p>
<p>|---|---|</p>
