<p>| Working medium | Water (closed cycle) |</p>
<p>| Startup energy | From any external source (grid, diesel, solar, wind) |</p>
<p>| Efficiency | Over 130% COP (claimed under specific conditions) |</p>
<p>| Emissions / waste / noise | None |</p>
<p>| Consumables and staffing | None required |</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Entire generator system housed within a 40-foot container: closed water loop, turbine-generator set, and startup interface accepting any external power source.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>No fuel or consumables required. Operates silently. Zero waste or emissions. Can be left unattended. Easy deployment even in hard-to-reach areas. Provides green, autonomous, and stable power where conventional grids are unavailable, unreliable, or environmentally unsuitable.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Off-Grid Power Systems · Closed-Cycle Hydropower · Autonomous Energy Units</p></section>
