<p>Shredded LIB material is fed to a mercury bath where metals dissolve into an amalgam; under deep vacuum the mercury evaporates at ambient temperature and is condensed back (closed loop, loss &lt;1 %), leaving the metals to separate by density (gravity stratification). No furnace, no acid leaching.</p>
