<p>| POME wastewater | none | generated |</p>
<p>| Methane emissions | none | generated |</p>
<p>| Waste disposal cost eliminated | $50–100/t | — |</p>
<p>| Total daily oil output at scale | 297 t/day | 237.6 t/day |</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Vertical 20-foot tank occupying 20 m²; grinding stage for fresh fruit bunches; water mixing; deep-vacuum separation chamber operating at ambient temperature; oil fraction collection for CPO and PKO; water recycling circuit; dry residue discharge. Full automation with pressure, temperature and level sensors.</p>
<p>Modular: units operate standalone or integrate into existing mills; five units replace a conventional plant.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Product: higher yield — 59.4 t/day against 53; cleaner oil with low acidity; carotenes and tocopherols retained because there is no thermal stage.</p>
<p>Economic: CAPEX 2.7× lower, OPEX 33× lower; $50–100 per tonne of waste disposal cost eliminated; one operator per unit.</p>
<p>Process: 5 kWh/t against 15–20; no steam, solvents or reagents; FFB processed without pre-separation; 24/7 automated operation with maintenance limited to pump checks and residue unloading.</p>
<p>Environmental: zero emissions; no POME, which is the principal environmental liability of conventional palm milling; no methane; water recycled; residue converted to bio-coal or feed.</p>
<p>Logistics: 20 m² footprint enables on-site processing at the plantation, cutting transport of bulky fresh fruit bunches.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>ARBOK-Palm Solid Fuel (PSF) · Arbok-Sun-Oily · ARBOK-VC (Vacuum Cracking) · ARBOK-BioProtein (ABP) · ARBOK-FRYLOOP</p>
<p>Integrates into existing mills or operates standalone. Dry residue feeds the bio-coal and feed lines; recovered water returns to production.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Deployment: standalone compact units at the plantation, or integration into an existing mill. Scaling by unit count — five units for 1,080 tonnes FFB/day.</p>
<p>Operation: fully automated, 24/7, one operator per unit. Maintenance limited to pump checks and residue unloading.</p>
<p>Commercial model: BOT over 15 years quoted for the five-unit configuration; also available for projects, licensing or partnership.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 7</strong> — проставлен Михаилом 2026-08-06.</p>
<p>Validated through industrial trials confirming efficiency, safety and environmental compliance. Certified for food and industrial applications. Stated ready for immediate deployment.</p>
<p>Formal TRL rating:</p></section>
