<p>Coal is gasified to syngas (CO + H₂); during cooling/condensation, heavy hydrocarbon condensates form (hydrocarbons, water, ash, polymerized organics). These are routed to an Arbok-ZWD unit under deep vacuum, where they separate by volatility and density — no reagents or filtration — into three streams: high-octane hydrocarbon blendstock (stabilized hydrocarbon phase), technical water, and solid ash/carbon concentrate.</p>
