        'seo_description' => 'BUTANOIL is an innovative green technology for converting livestock and sewage waste into high-quality butyl alcohol (butanol) — a clean, energy-efficient…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>BUTANOIL is an innovative green technology for converting livestock and sewage waste into high-quality butyl alcohol (butanol) — a clean, energy-efficient biofuel. The process is based on proprietary enzymatic fermentation with no distillation, pyrolysis, or synthetic chemicals, using unique strains of yeast and fungi. Unlike traditional methods such as methane biogas plants, BUTANOIL does not leave behind toxic sludge or require expensive infrastructure. It uses liquid organic waste — pig manure, biogas slurry, and municipal sewage — and transforms it into a valuable, ready-to-use fuel. The conversion process takes 8–10 weeks and yields up to 12% butanol by volume; the resulting dry residue is odorless, toxin-free humus, or can be pressed into bio-briquettes (8–14 MJ/kg) worth up to $125/ton.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Integration into existing farms, municipal waste treatment plants, or mini-refineries. Agricultural use: machinery fuel, power generation, fertilizer production.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Proprietary enzymatic fermentation using unique strains of yeast and fungi, without distillation, pyrolysis, or synthetic chemicals. Liquid organic waste (pig manure, biogas slurry, municipal sewage, organic residues) is fermented over 8–10 weeks, yielding up to 12% butyl alcohol by volume. The dry residue is odorless, toxin-free humus, or is pressed into bio-briquettes.</p></section>
