<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Enzymatic fermentation stage using proprietary yeast and fungal strains; butanol recovery; solid residue drying and briquette pressing. Compatible with existing storage and processing equipment; no distillation or pyrolysis units required.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Butanol is comparable to gasoline in power and application while emitting 80% less CO₂ (2.38 g/g vs 6.18 g/g). Safe and natural process with no toxic emissions and no toxic sludge. Dual-output system delivering fuel plus dry organic fertilizer or bio-briquettes. No expensive infrastructure required. Significantly reduces GHG emissions, enabling the sale of carbon credits, and turns waste disposal into a profitable fuel production cycle.</p></section>
