        'source_file' => 'DEKA.md',
        'sector_slug' => 'sector-c',
        'sector_name' => 'Energy Production',
        'readiness_slug' => 'trl-4-5',
        'readiness_label' => 'TRL 5',
        'short_description' => 'ARBOK-DEKA is an electrochemical electricity generator that runs on slightly salted water (including seawater) plus a specialized, long-life replaceable metal cartridge (proprietary know-how).',
        'seo_title' => 'ARBOK-DEKA | ARBOK Technology',
        'seo_description' => 'ARBOK-DEKA is an electrochemical electricity generator that runs on slightly salted water (including seawater) plus a specialized, long-life replaceable…',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ARBOK-DEKA is an electrochemical electricity generator that runs on slightly salted water (including seawater) plus a specialized, long-life replaceable metal cartridge (proprietary know-how). Water is a minimal-consumable input and the cartridge cost is negligible per kWh. Containerized (20/40-ft) or wheeled, it suits remote, off-grid areas (deserts, isolated villages) where fuel delivery is impractical, and smaller units power yachts, boats, and ships. It needs no fuel and is far cheaper than combustion generators.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Primary use cases: off-grid power for remote villages and desert sites; marine power (yachts, boats, ships — networks or propulsion); emergency/autonomous power.</p>
<p>Industries and users: off-grid communities, marine operators, remote industry.</p>
<p>Scale: 5 kW DC (20-ft) / 10 kW DC (40-ft); smaller marine units.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Electrochemical reaction between slightly salted/seawater and a specialized metal cartridge generates DC electricity; water is a minimal consumable and the cartridge is replaceable (months-to-years life). No combustion, no fuel.</p>
<p>Limitations: R&amp;D stage; cartridge supply/replacement; DC output needs inverter for AC.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>Input: slightly salted water or seawater. Cartridge: single replaceable metal unit, long life. Output: 5 kW DC (20-ft) / 10 kW DC (40-ft); ~7–12 kW AC (inverter-dependent). Housing: 20/40-ft container or wheeled. Zero fuel; minimal consumables.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Electrochemical cell with metal cartridge; saltwater feed; DC output + inverter; control system; containerized or chassis-mounted. Cartridge replaceable.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Technical: fuel-free; runs on seawater; long-life cartridge; container/wheeled deployment.</p>
