        'seo_description' => 'ORGAPHAN is an organic packaging material that is both fully biodegradable and edible, aimed at replacing petrochemical-polymer packaging waste.',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ORGAPHAN is an organic packaging material that is both fully biodegradable and edible, aimed at replacing petrochemical-polymer packaging waste. Made from simple, fast-renewing organic raw materials and food-production by-products, it is designed for plastic-like structural durability while remaining compostable and safe for consumption.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Food and goods packaging; eco-friendly wrapping in hospitality/catering; compostable multi-layer covers for household goods, furniture casings, and appliance covers. Customizable with organic dyes and flavorings.</p>
<p>Users: food/retail packaging, hospitality, consumer-goods sectors.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Operating Principle</h2><p>Fast-renewing organic raw materials and food-process by-products are formed into a structurally durable yet fully compostable and ingestible film/material, optionally multi-layered for stiffer applications. Provides plastic-like resilience with far lower ecological impact.</p>
<p>Limitations: source card lacks quantitative parameters; mechanical, barrier, and shelf-life properties are undocumented and unvalidated.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Key Parameters</h2><p>Edible and food-safe; fully biodegradable with no harmful residues; plastic-comparable resilience; multi-layer configurations; customizable dyes/flavorings; made from renewable biomass + food by-products.</p>
<p>Note: no numeric parameters (strength, barrier, biodegradation time, shelf life) are given in the source — these must be defined and measured.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Architecture and Components</h2><p>Organic film/material from renewable biomass and food by-products; optional multi-layer build-up; optional organic dye/flavor additives. Composition not specified in source.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Advantages</h2><p>Technical: plastic-like durability while edible and compostable; multi-layer adaptability. Economic: uses low-cost waste from other organic processes. Environmental: reduces plastic waste, food-safe end-of-life (compost or ingestion), supports circular economy.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Fits food/goods packaging lines and hospitality wrapping; complements ARBOK bio-materials and waste-valorization platforms.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Deployment &amp; Operation</h2><p>Steps: source organic feedstock/by-products → form material (single or multi-layer) → apply to packaging use case. Remaining: define and test mechanical/barrier properties, move from early prototypes to pilot production (funding/partnership-dependent).</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>TRL</h2><p><strong>TRL 3 (confirmed by Michael).</strong> Experimental proof-of-concept: early prototypes and materials testing completed, with pilot production pending funding/partnerships and core properties still undocumented. (Matches the card&#x27;s &quot;R&amp;D&quot; status.)</p>
<p>TRL scale:</p>
