<li>Pursue regulatory approvals in target markets (India, China, Middle East, North Africa)</li>
</ul></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Market Potential</h2><p><strong>Target markets:</strong> Cities with chronic smog problems (South Asia, East Asia, Middle East, Latin America, Eastern Europe); airports with frequent fog delays; highway corridors with inversion-related accident clusters</p>
<p><strong>Global market size:</strong> Air pollution costs global economies ~$5–8 trillion annually in health, productivity, and infrastructure losses; urban air quality management is a $multi-billion addressable market</p>
<p><strong>Key drivers:</strong> WHO air quality standards tightening; growing urban populations; increasing frequency of wildfire smoke and dust storm events; aviation delay economics; government liability for pollution-related health costs</p></section>
