        'seo_description' => 'ZERROFAT breaks down fat molecules in food that has already been cooked.',
        'content_html' => '<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>ZERROFAT breaks down fat molecules in food that has already been cooked. The process destroys low-density and very-low-density lipoproteins, and fat content in the treated dish is reduced to zero percent. The broken-down fat molecules are converted into amino acids, which the body absorbs readily without forming fat deposits.</p>
<p>The point of the device is that it acts after cooking rather than before: the food is prepared normally, then treated. Texture, taste, colour and aroma are unaltered — the source states that appearance and sensory qualities before and after treatment are virtually indistinguishable. Treatment takes approximately one minute and the temperature of the food remains unchanged.</p>
<p>Physically the device resembles a conventional microwave oven and is intended for both households and food service establishments, enabling menus labelled 0 % FAT.</p></section>
<section class="arbok-imported-section"><h2>Applications</h2><p>Domestic use in households. Food service establishments offering 0 % FAT menu options. Industrial food processing. Weight management without restrictive diets — the source states that consistent use of ZERROFAT-processed food can produce weight loss without dietary restriction or specialized diets.</p></section>
